            "文档",
            "研究",
            "评审",
            "定时"
          ],
          "description": "ordinary conversation kind"
        },
        "topic": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "ordinary topic, at most 14 characters"
        },
        "user_asked": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "explicit user request to replace their title/name"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "conversation_archive",
    "description": "Archive a Persona conversation: it leaves the sidebar's list (it is kept, and listed under 已归档), nothing is deleted. Only when the user asks to tidy up or archive. The main conversation can't be archived. Archiving this conversation itself is allowed: the current turn finishes, and a new message from the user brings it back.\n\nWrite newly generated user-facing arguments, such as titles, reasons, criteria and messages, in English unless the user requests another language or the field requires source wording. Preserve quoted source text, identifiers, tool and parameter names, enum values and command prefixes exactly. Language does not change approval requirements or permission boundaries.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "full id or its first 8 characters"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "conversation_unarchive",
    "description": "Bring an archived Persona conversation back into the sidebar's list (find it with conversations_list and include_archived).\n\nWrite newly generated user-facing arguments, such as titles, reasons, criteria and messages, in English unless the user requests another language or the field requires source wording. Preserve quoted source text, identifiers, tool and parameter names, enum values and command prefixes exactly. Language does not change approval requirements or permission boundaries.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "full id or its first 8 characters"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "conversation_tags_set",
    "description": "Replace a conversation's tags; [] clears them. These user-defined labels group conversations in apps and lists. They are trimmed and de-duplicated, at most 10 of 32 characters each. Tag only conversations in your own space when the user asks for tags or grouping; never invent them. This conversation is a valid id.\n\nWrite newly generated user-facing arguments, such as titles, reasons, criteria and messages, in English unless the user requests another language or the field requires source wording. Preserve quoted source text, identifiers, tool and parameter names, enum values and command prefixes exactly. Language does not change approval requirements or permission boundaries.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "tags"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "full id or first 8 characters"
        },
        "tags": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "complete replacement list; [] clears all"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "conversation_new",
    "description": "Open a chat the owner requested. Returns its ID and preset configuration. It reports via conversation_send; failure or silence leaves one notice. Respect read-only refusals.\n\nWrite newly generated user-facing arguments, such as titles, reasons, criteria and messages, in English unless the user requests another language or the field requires source wording. Preserve quoted source text, identifiers, tool and parameter names, enum values and command prefixes exactly. Language does not change approval requirements or permission boundaries.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "text"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "text": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Self-contained first message"
        },
        "tags": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "Only if asked; up to 10 tags, 32 characters each"
        },
        "tier": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Active profile preset; unknown or assistant-incompatible presets are refused"
        },
        "pin": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "Ask for approval to pin after the first turn"
        },
        "quote": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "“latest”, a message ID or the owner’s exact words"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "conversation_send",
    "description": "Message another conversation; it waits for a running turn or 2 min of user quiet. Replies use conversation_send. Few hops per user message (main: no cap; a wake-up resets; a first reply adds none). Past the rate it queues: the result says when. Ack or FYI only: wake false. Follow policy refusals; don't retry. Owner-verbatim words to main: start with them. Handing on a user request: set quote (free once).\n\nWrite newly generated user-facing arguments, such as titles, reasons, criteria and messages, in English unless the user requests another language or the field requires source wording. Preserve quoted source text, identifiers, tool and parameter names, enum values and command prefixes exactly. Language does not change approval requirements or permission boundaries.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "text"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "full id or its first 8 characters"
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "quote": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "\"latest\" (this turn), a message id or the user's exact words"
        },
        "wake": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "false: no turn; read with the next one"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "task_plan",
    "description": "Use task_plan for code, repo research and multi-step work (one task per independent piece). Check machines_list, KB, agents_list and preferences for editable choices and one-line reasons. Main/lead plans start at once; elsewhere read-only, user_requested and preapproved kinds do; others and owner_step wait for 开始. Queued receipt means dispatched; check the to-do outcome and use agent_send.\n\nFixed machine_policy stays on that machine and refuses unavailable launchers; flexible moves portable work on failed health checks (explain why). Planning leads own their tasks: signals, cards, start remedies, review and cancellation. Main owns its tasks and receives needs_user escalations. Main may select a lead; agent_transfer persists ownership. An incompatible lead must gain supervision_policy before starting work. Check returned supervisor and similar work. Pass todo_id for caller's unassigned to-do (Lark topic, split, failed start).\n\nStarted tasks keep a hub brief (owner request or started_why). Give goal, done_when, out_of_bounds: writable needs done_when (PR/Issue defaults to merged+closed unless PR/draft-only); read-only needs goal. Omit expect_minutes for auto estimate; positive overrides (manual Agents lack estimate_due). Use continues+continues_why to continue, task_retry for failed starts, task_scope+scope_revision for approved changes.\n\nEdits need readonly=false and authorized write permission; replace read-only Codex with writable for fixes, or use agent_send when permissions match. readonly=true adds the read-only constraint. Claude-family uses bypassPermissions for both; Codex uses plan unless assistant.readonly_mode=prompt; pi/cursor/agy refuse readonly. Set role=worker, or leader for direct workers via restricted task_plan/task_review (workers cannot delegate).\n\nResolve repository identity via repositories_list (repository_get only when useful). The user's explicit repository URL or path takes precedence. A saved binding is a reference, not authorization; never infer a machine or checkout path from it. Non-repository tasks need no lookup; retrieval is not a mandatory dispatch preflight. Closing the terminal on acceptance is the owner's choice; this tool cannot set it.\n\nFor a saved workspace naming plan on an existing todo, select {\"backend\":{\"operation_id\":\"\u003cid\u003e\"}}. For a multi-repo container workspace, select {\"container\":{\"selected_repo_ids\":[\"\u003crepo_id\u003e\",...]}} (or {\"container\":{\"operation_id\":\"\u003cid\u003e\"}} with todo_id for a prepared container). Optional host picks an enabled engine. All selected repos must be ready before start.\n\nWorkspace policy: \"new\" isolates a checkout; {\"new\":{\"branch\":\"task/my-change\"}} names its branch; {\"existing\":\"\u003ccwd or workspace_id\u003e\",\"queue\":true} picks one (queue:true or owner in after queues FIFO and auto-starts when free; else busy refuses with owner); \"none\" creates nothing. Omitted: readonly uses none; writable Git follows assistant.task_workspace_preference (prefer-existing default, prefer-new to isolate), busy cwd uses new. Explicit existing never switches silently. Reusing explicit new branch needs clean checkout, no live Agent and no open owner, else refuse with path/owner. Engine owns creation/registration; never run git worktree add. Default branch: task/\u003ctodo id\u003e. Failed creation starts no Agent; workspaces stay after acceptance. Follow org read-only refusals; never retry unchanged.\n\n`wait_seconds` observes up to 50 seconds after dispatch, appending `Inline observation` JSON: `completed`(this input's `reply`), `question`(pending `interaction_id`), `timeout`/`cancelled`/`unavailable`/`interrupted`/`failed`, with known input/session ids. Observation never answers questions, accepts tasks, resends or cancels work; normal supervision/`task_review` applies. Older nodes may time out rather than return an unrelated reply. Only an immediately dispatchable single-task plan waits; approval cards and multi-task plans return immediately.\n\nWrite newly generated user-facing arguments, such as titles, reasons, criteria and messages, in English unless the user requests another language or the field requires source wording. Preserve quoted source text, identifiers, tool and parameter names, enum values and command prefixes exactly. Language does not change approval requirements or permission boundaries.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "tasks"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "wait_seconds": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0,
          "description": "0/omitted: normal receipt"
        },
        "supervisor": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "optional current leader id (assistant.leaders), selected by main; omitted: the planning lead, otherwise main"
        },
        "tasks": {
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 1,
          "maxItems": 8,
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "title",
              "prompt",
              "role",
              "machine",
              "readonly",
              "user_requested",
              "why"
            ],
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "required": [
                  "cwd"
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "workspace",
                  "todo_id"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "workspace": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "backend"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "workspace"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "workspace": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "container"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              }
            ],
            "properties": {
              "title": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Card title in English, under 20 characters."
              },
              "context": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "extra facts; no project background"
              },
              "prompt": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "goal, bounds and facts; manager adds context, criteria and rules"
              },
              "skip_project_memory": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "description": "default false; true skips project/direction memory; prompt unchanged"
              },
              "machine": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Machine id; fixed by default."
              },
              "machine_policy": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "fixed",
                  "flexible"
                ],
                "description": "fixed (default): keep this machine; flexible: permit health-based moves only for portable work"
              },
              "cwd": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Absolute or ~/ project dir, unless workspace.backend or workspace.container supplies it."
              },
              "workspace": {
                "type": [
                  "string",
                  "object"
                ],
                "description": "workspace policy; omit for default; existing: abs/~/path or workspace id on that machine; no custom root",
                "oneOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "string",
                    "enum": [
                      "new",
                      "none"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "backend"
                    ],
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "properties": {
                      "backend": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "required": [
                          "operation_id"
                        ],
                        "additionalProperties": false,
                        "properties": {
                          "operation_id": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "minLength": 1
                          },
                          "host": {
                            "type": "string"
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "container"
                    ],
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "properties": {
                      "container": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "additionalProperties": false,
                        "properties": {
                          "selected_repo_ids": {
                            "type": "array",
                            "minItems": 1,
                            "items": {
                              "type": "string",
                              "minLength": 1
                            }
                          },
                          "operation_id": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "minLength": 1
                          },
                          "host": {
                            "type": "string"
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "existing"
                    ],
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "properties": {
                      "existing": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "minLength": 1
                      },
                      "queue": {
                        "type": "boolean"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "new"
                    ],
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "properties": {
                      "new": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "additionalProperties": false,
                        "properties": {
                          "branch": {
                            "type": "string"
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "launcher": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "listed launcher (Claude Code, pi, cursor or agy in herdr); unknown names refused with choices; empty: default/fallback, claude first, why says which"
              },
              "model": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "model id or alias the agent takes; empty: the launcher's default"
              },
              "permission": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "default",
                  "acceptEdits",
                  "plan",
                  "auto",
                  "bypassPermissions"
                ],
                "description": "mode; empty: writable default; readonly/replacement/Codex rules: see description; TRAE CLI and omp take none"
              },
              "role": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "worker",
                  "leader"
                ],
                "description": "worker: ordinary; leader (any conversation): starts/reviews direct workers"
              },
              "ultracode": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "description": "large tasks (many files, multi-angle checks): Claude Code multi-agent workflows, slower/costlier; small tasks: false; Claude Code 2.1.284+ only; never put in prompt/title"
              },
              "readonly": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "description": "true only for a task that must remain read-only; false for explicitly authorized file changes (a Codex read-only sandbox: see the description). The first message adds「本任务只读：不改项目文件、不提交、不对外写入」 only when true"
              },
              "user_requested": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "description": "True only if the user's latest message asked for it; else false."
              },
              "owner_step": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "money",
                  "outward",
                  "irreversible"
                ],
                "description": "money, speaking as the user, or an unagreed irreversible step"
              },
              "why": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "One-line reason in English for the machine, directory and model."
              },
              "done_when": {
                "type": "array",
                "maxItems": 6,
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "description": "Checkable acceptance results in English, one per entry, shared with the Agent. Nonempty for writable tasks; ignored with continues."
              },
              "goal": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Owner's one-line outcome in English. Required for read-only tasks; writable tasks default to the title."
              },
              "out_of_bounds": {
                "type": "array",
                "maxItems": 6,
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "description": "Optional forbidden actions or areas in English, one per entry."
              },
              "continues": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Original todo id. Reuse todo, original brief and effective criteria even on failed Start; never split. Start stops/releases active prior Agents and reopens if closed. Refuse unauthorized takeover, unreachable Agents that cannot be stopped, or open legacy successors."
              },
              "scope_revision": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "With continues after a scope change: exact task_scope scope_revision; refuse stale plans."
              },
              "continues_why": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "With continues: one-line stop/replacement reason saved on this plan."
              },
              "started_why": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "If not just owner-requested (own idea, 督办 or routine): one-line start reason saved in brief."
              },
              "attachments": {
                "type": "array",
                "maxItems": 8,
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "description": "abs paths of pictures/files user gave in this chat (Claude Code path or app attachment); copied to agent with updated mentions; others refused"
              },
              "expect_minutes": {
                "type": "integer",
                "minimum": 0,
                "description": "Optional minutes override. Omit/0: comparable history, or the 60-minute system_default; positive: override. Review at 1×; stuck at 1.5× (min 20m); overdue at 3× (min 24h)."
              },
              "project": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Existing kb_list projects slug/name for a clear long-term area; no near-duplicates."
              },
              "part_of": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Optional request todo this is a piece of."
              },
              "after": {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "description": "With part_of: prerequisite pieces."
              },
              "todo_id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Open or failed-start todo this chat opened/supervises; no live Agent. Release stopped Agents at Start. Equals continues if both are given."
              },
              "inbox_item": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Handed-off Inbox ID, or 'none' for unrelated work. Checks the conversation and manager; links without filing or replying."
              },
              "tier": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Agent preset from the snapshot's 模型档位 line; choose by purpose; resolved at task start with its profile; explicit launcher/model/effort/speed overrides"
              },
              "speed": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "standard",
                  "fast",
                  "ultrafast"
                ],
                "description": "new-start speed; standard/omitted: launcher default. Codex: fast, ultrafast; Claude Code: fast only"
              },
              "effort": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Explicit effort; omit for tier/purpose default."
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "task_plan_withdraw",
    "description": "Take down a plan card this conversation put up (task_plan) while nothing of it has started: its work was done elsewhere, or the user decided not to do it. The card stops waiting for the user's 开始, as when they dismiss it themselves, and leaves the to-handle lists (the snapshot's plans waiting to start, the briefings). Only for a plan of this conversation that still waits for 开始; a started or dismissed plan, or another conversation's, is refused and nothing changes. Your reason is kept on record; tell the user in a line which card you took down and why.\n\nWrite newly generated user-facing arguments, such as titles, reasons, criteria and messages, in English unless the user requests another language or the field requires source wording. Preserve quoted source text, identifiers, tool and parameter names, enum values and command prefixes exactly. Language does not change approval requirements or permission boundaries.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "plan_id",
        "reason"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "plan_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the plan's id (plan_…), as task_plan's answer or the snapshot's plans waiting to start give it"
        },
        "reason": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "why it is no longer needed, in the user's language, one sentence"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "task_review",
    "description": "accepted closes work after the delivery gate (default delivery_gate=merged: park verified open PRs; linked issues must close). user_check keeps the task and Agent open until owner Pass and routes feedback to that Agent. If opted in at Start, accepted done cleans up the idle tab unless user_check. Report closed/skipped/pending; never close the tab yourself. rework caps stalled/low-ROI churn at 2 rounds (external_input/substantive_new cap at 10 total); accept with a brief note instead of bouncing for low-ROI edge cases or style nitpicks. Replace stopped Agents via agent_start. Use parked with evidence for external waits and needs_user if only the owner can contact, approve, or trigger work.\n\nFor accepted (outcome=done), include each done_when criterion once in checks (met=true, nonblank evidence), even with user_check. outcome=cannot, cancelled and no-criteria tasks are unchanged. Other verdicts can omit checks and keep progress. Report each criterion met/not_met/dropped, then also_done. Judge the scoped brief over handovers or Agent claims.\n\nGive accepted outcome/reason/link. The hub sends conclusion cards and passes verification unless user_check. needs_user can default to recommend at 24h/deadline. Irreversible or visible_to_others only remind. Recheck at 24h. “You decide”, “This isn't what I asked for” and “Tell me the background first” return to supervision. Clarify without repeating or acting irreversibly/externally.\n\nA non-main reviewer of another supervisor's task may only accept/cancel; send gaps via agent_send. A leader's needs_user reaches main too. Cancel only duplicates/unwanted tasks; their Agents close/archive and cards end.\n\nWrite newly generated user-facing arguments, such as titles, reasons, criteria and messages, in English unless the user requests another language or the field requires source wording. Preserve quoted source text, identifiers, tool and parameter names, enum values and command prefixes exactly. Language does not change approval requirements or permission boundaries.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "todo_id",
        "verdict"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "todo_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the task's todo id (todo_…), from the 督办 message or the context snapshot"
        },
        "verdict": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "accepted",
            "rework",
            "needs_user",
            "parked",
            "cancelled"
          ]
        },
        "rework_kind": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "external_input",
            "substantive_new",
            "repeated_error",
            "low_roi_edge"
          ],
          "description": "rework, optional: external_input (external review/conflict/owner input; skips 2-round stalled cap), substantive_new (prior gap fixed, new defect found; resets stalled cap), repeated_error/low_roi_edge (default when omitted; cap 2 stalled, 10 total)"
        },
        "checks": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "criterion",
              "met"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "criterion": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "one done_when criterion (or what the task was for, when it had none)"
              },
              "met": {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              "evidence": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "what shows it is met (a link, a command's output), or what is missing"
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "each criterion (met or not) with evidence/gap; updates persisted state, evidence, time, and supervisor. Omitted entries keep progress"
        },
        "note": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "rework: what the agent is to do (English, concrete); needs_user: what the user is to decide; parked: anything more than reason, for your own record; cancelled: why; accepted: the result in a line"
        },
        "outcome": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "done",
            "cannot"
          ],
          "description": "accepted: done (work complete or answer yes) or cannot (proved impossible); default done"
        },
        "reason": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "one sentence in the user's language: accepted (why; default note's first line), needs_user (required: what to decide), or parked (required: what it waits for; include PR link if waiting on a PR)"
        },
        "waiting_on": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "someone_else",
            "external_event",
            "date"
          ],
          "description": "parked (required): someone_else (person acts/answers), external_event (outside event), or date. Owner decisions use needs_user; legacy owner_priority parks stay readable"
        },
        "until": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "parked, optional: duration (\"3d\", \"36h\", \"90m\") or RFC 3339 time, 1m–30d ahead; default 24h. waiting_on=date requires explicit RFC 3339"
        },
        "link": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "accepted/needs_user: one evidence link (PR/page/doc); defaults to task PR, note/checks link, or agent chat"
        },
        "recommend": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "needs_user (required): recommended option label (first in options); owner OK sends it to the agent"
        },
        "why_owner": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "irreversible",
            "visible_to_others",
            "priority",
            "acceptance",
            "only_owner_knows"
          ],
          "description": "needs_user (required): irreversible (delete/prod write/spend), visible_to_others (external message/comment/review), priority (whether/order), acceptance (visual check), only_owner_knows (private fact); decide anything else yourself"
        },
        "options": {
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 2,
          "maxItems": 4,
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "label",
              "leads_to"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "label": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "the option in a few words, as a button says it"
              },
              "leads_to": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "one sentence: what choosing it leads to"
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "needs_user (required): 2–4 options, recommended first"
        },
        "cost_of_waiting": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "needs_user (required): one sentence saying what it costs if the user does not answer soon"
        },
        "question_quote": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "needs_user: the Agent's question verbatim when reason paraphrases it (hub checks for an existing reply)"
        },
        "can_wait": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "needs_user, optional: defer to next daily briefing (low cost, nobody blocked today, no deadline \u003c12h); no push/card, listed in Needs you. Ignored for irreversible/visible_to_others, deadline \u003c12h, reversible=false, or no briefing with facts due within 24h and \u003e=12h before deadline; default false"
        },
        "deadline": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "needs_user, optional: how long the decision waits, duration (\"4h\") or RFC 3339 time, 1m–30d ahead; needs reversible. Default 24h reversible; none for why_owner irreversible/visible_to_others"
        },
        "also_done": {
          "type": "array",
          "maxItems": 6,
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "accepted, optional: what was done beyond the task's brief (one line each); the task's page lists it after the criteria"
        },
        "withdraw_needs_user": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "accepted only, task in needs_user: its supervisor or main takes it back and closes it silently (no card/push)"
        },
        "user_check": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "accepted only: user must inspect result (e.g. UI change); shows \"Please verify\" card awaiting \"Pass\" instead of auto-passing; default false"
        },
        "reversible": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "with deadline: whether taking recommend can be undone; false for delete/external send/spend/prod change (never auto-taken; required false for irreversible/visible_to_others)"
        },
        "evidence": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "kind",
            "target",
            "wake",
            "next_actor"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "kind": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "person_reply",
                "merge_review",
                "external_event",
                "date"
              ],
              "description": "External wait kind"
            },
            "target": {
              "type": "string",
              "maxLength": 200,
              "description": "The person or external object"
            },
            "wake": {
              "type": "string",
              "maxLength": 600,
              "description": "Observable change that ends the wait"
            },
            "next_actor": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "external",
                "owner"
              ],
              "description": "external: third party, system or time, without a prior owner step. owner: use needs_user"
            },
            "url": {
              "type": "string",
              "maxLength": 2000,
              "description": "Required for merge_review (ready PR/MR) and external_event"
            },
            "interaction_id": {
              "type": "string",
              "maxLength": 200,
              "description": "external_event only. This worker's exact pending owner request ID from agents_list. Shows the existing request"
            },
            "pr_event": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "terminal",
                "terminal_or_review"
              ],
              "description": "GitHub PR waits only. terminal for merge or close. terminal_or_review adds new submitted reviews"
            },
            "contact": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "channel",
                "url",
                "sender",
                "sent_at",
                "request",
                "status"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "channel": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "maxLength": 100
                },
                "url": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "maxLength": 2000,
                  "description": "sent-message/receipt link, not a channel homepage"
                },
                "sender": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "maxLength": 200
                },
                "sent_at": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "date-time",
                  "description": "actual sent time; not in the future"
                },
                "request": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "maxLength": 600
                },
                "status": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "sent"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "description": "Sent request, required for person_reply and merge_review"
            },
            "ready": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "enum": [
                true
              ],
              "description": "merge_review only. The PR/MR is ready for the reviewer"
            },
            "reply": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "source",
                "brand",
                "app_id",
                "account_open_id",
                "person_open_id",
                "chat_id",
                "thread_id",
                "request_message_id"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "source": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "larkcli"
                  ]
                },
                "brand": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "feishu",
                    "lark"
                  ]
                },
                "app_id": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "account_open_id": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "person_open_id": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "expected human OpenID in this app, not self"
                },
                "chat_id": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "thread_id": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "provider topic ID, not root-message ID"
                },
                "request_message_id": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "description": "person_reply: exact IDs from a configured lark-cli reader, never names. contact.url must be the sent request's matching topic AppLink. A verified reply asks the current supervisor to review, not direct Agent delivery"
            }
          },
          "description": "Required for parked. Inspect the source. recorded_by is output only. Missing legacy evidence is unverified"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "task_scope",
    "description": "Change what a supervised task is to do, or what done means, after it started (its todo id). The brief is never rewritten: this adds a brief-log entry (what changed and why), applies the new done_when/expect_minutes, restarts overdue, estimate_due only on a new estimate; the owner reads it in the next digest. It is the only way done_when changes after start (agent_supervise and agent_send on a task use the same log). Give done_when as the whole list after the change: a criterion you leave out is logged as dropped and named in the completion report. A change adding an owner-only step (deploying, merging, releasing, public sends/comments, deleting, spending, production changes) not in the original task is refused unless the owner's own message started this turn: ask first (ask_user, or task_review needs_user), then call again. Only its supervisor may call it; the Agent is not told — send the change with agent_send. estimate_due/overdue: revise expect_minutes here, but a finished task past the settle window with no owner card is refused: give task_review first (accepted/rework/cancelled; needs_user or accepted+user_check if the owner must act); chat-only asks never reach Needs you.\n\nWrite newly generated user-facing arguments, such as titles, reasons, criteria and messages, in English unless the user requests another language or the field requires source wording. Preserve quoted source text, identifiers, tool and parameter names, enum values and command prefixes exactly. Language does not change approval requirements or permission boundaries.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "todo_id",
        "change",
        "why"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "todo_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the task's todo id (todo_…)"
        },
        "change": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "what changes, in one sentence the owner can read (English), e.g. require verification in the test environment only, instead of a staged production rollout"
        },
        "why": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "why, in one sentence (English)"
        },
        "done_when": {
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 1,
          "maxItems": 6,
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "the criteria after the change, the whole list; leave it out to keep them as they are"
        },
        "expect_minutes": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0,
          "description": "how long the task should take from now; leave it out (or 0) to keep it"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "task_decided",
    "description": "Record the owner's needs_user choice; main chat or supervisor only. Quote their words and exact option; never guess. told_agent=true means already delivered (also direct Agent chat): record only. Otherwise send and record. Both settle the ask.\n\nWrite newly generated user-facing arguments, such as titles, reasons, criteria and messages, in English unless the user requests another language or the field requires source wording. Preserve quoted source text, identifiers, tool and parameter names, enum values and command prefixes exactly. Language does not change approval requirements or permission boundaries.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "todo_id",
        "option",
        "said"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "todo_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "task id"
        },
        "option": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "exact option label"
        },
        "said": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "owner's words"
        },
        "told_agent": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "true: already delivered to the Agent, record only; false: relay and record"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "task_start_screen",
    "description": "Read the last 30 lines of the terminal tab a task's agent did not start in, while its computer keeps that tab (a 督办 message says until when): the question the tab's shell waits on, or where the agent's own screen stopped. Only for a task of this conversation whose start is being remedied; what it shows stays here, it is not kept with the task.\n\nWrite newly generated user-facing arguments, such as titles, reasons, criteria and messages, in English unless the user requests another language or the field requires source wording. Preserve quoted source text, identifiers, tool and parameter names, enum values and command prefixes exactly. Language does not change approval requirements or permission boundaries.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "todo_id"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "todo_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the task's id, as the 督办 message gives it"
        },
        "reason": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "why you look, in the user's language (optional; kept with the task's history)"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "task_start_keys",
    "description": "Type into the terminal tab a task's agent did not start in, while its computer keeps that tab and no agent runs there: text as is (no enter, at most 32 characters), then keys by name (\"enter\", \"esc\", \"ctrl+c\", \"y\", \"n\", \"up\", \"down\"…, at most 8). Use it to answer the question the tab's shell waits on, or to get past where the agent's screen stopped; read the tab first with task_start_screen and again after. The keys, the text and your reason are kept with the task's history. It starts nothing: start the agent again with task_retry.\n\nWrite newly generated user-facing arguments, such as titles, reasons, criteria and messages, in English unless the user requests another language or the field requires source wording. Preserve quoted source text, identifiers, tool and parameter names, enum values and command prefixes exactly. Language does not change approval requirements or permission boundaries.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "todo_id",
        "reason"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "todo_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the task's id, as the 督办 message gives it"
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "string",
          "maxLength": 32,
          "description": "text to type as is, before the keys"
        },
        "keys": {
          "type": "array",
          "maxItems": 8,
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "keys to press after the text, by name"
        },
        "reason": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "why these keys, in the user's language, one sentence"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "task_retry",
    "description": "Start a failed task's agent again: in its kept tab (once task_start_keys answered what stopped it), else in a new tab, reopening it; with launcher, on that launcher of the same computer and workspace. At most 3 retries; the hub never retries itself. Returns at once; the outcome comes as a 督办 message. Only this conversation's tasks; reason goes in their history.\n\nWrite newly generated user-facing arguments, such as titles, reasons, criteria and messages, in English unless the user requests another language or the field requires source wording. Preserve quoted source text, identifiers, tool and parameter names, enum values and command prefixes exactly. Language does not change approval requirements or permission boundaries.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "todo_id",
        "reason"
      ],
      "properties": {
